# Environment variables for the Frontend Standard Template.
#
# ## Doppler (recommended)
# This project uses Doppler for secret management. When the Doppler CLI is
# installed and authenticated, `make dev` / `make build` inject secrets
# automatically via `doppler run`. No .env.local file is needed.
#
# Setup:
#   doppler login
#   doppler setup --project frontend-standard-project --config dev --no-interactive
#
# ## Manual fallback
# If Doppler is not available, `make dev` / `make build` fall back to reading
# from `.env.local`. Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values.
#
# All Vite-exposed variables MUST use the VITE_ prefix to be available via
# `import.meta.env.VITE_*` (see vite.config.ts and src/vite-env.d.ts).
#
# NOTE: The template does not yet read any environment variables in src/.
# These are provided as the documented convention for the API consumer layer
# that future apps built from this template will use.

# Base URL of the backend API the SPA talks to.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
